Subject: [PATCH] initramfs: explicitly load the packaged diagnostic GPI module

Replacing lib/modules/msm_gpi.ko does not select it for normal first-stage
loading: the original normal modules.load and its dependency closure omit
GPI. Add the module to that list so the first-stage loader attempts the
packaged module and its modules.options before later vendor loading.
The existing dependency table supplies its providers. Parallel loading
means this list position does not guarantee the last execution position.

Use with the matching NULL-safe diagnostic msm_gpi.ko and its explicit
kexec_first_event_diag option. This moves GPI loading/probing into the
first-stage loading set; it does not fix the original command timeout or
prove that the module successfully initialized on the device.

This patch targets the unpacked diagnostic initramfs, not kernel source.

diff --git a/lib/modules/modules.load b/lib/modules/modules.load
--- a/lib/modules/modules.load
+++ b/lib/modules/modules.load
@@ -151,3 +151,4 @@
 oplus_mdmfeature.ko
 oplus_bsp_fpga_monitor.ko
 ipclite.ko
+msm_gpi.ko
